# No long dashes

Never write em dashes (U+2014), en dashes (U+2013), or other long dashes in any site text: posts, headlines, homepage links, captions, front matter, or UI copy.

When adapting a Medium post, replace every long dash on the way in. Do this for titles, body, lists, and references.

```text
# BAD
Case 1 — Defining Churn
misleading — or simply impossible
2019–2020

# GOOD
Case 1 - Defining Churn
misleading - or simply impossible
2019-2020
```

Leave math minus signs (U+2212) in formulas. Leave ASCII `--` in SQL comments and code.

A hook auto-replaces leftover long dashes after edits. Still write short hyphens yourself so the first draft is clean.
